      "writtenOn": "2017-09-07T20:52:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand the concern is that someone might accidentally use gpio_set_flags() to turn on/off a pullup or set direction and lose the wake flag.\n\nIt might be better to make some safer functions than gpio_set_flags().  For example:\n\ngpio_add_flags(signal, flags_to_add)\ngpio_sub_flags(signal, flags_to_remove)\n\nOr maybe:\n\ngpio_addsub_flags(signal, to_add, to_remove)\ngpio_change_flags(signal, mask, value)\n\nEither that, or we need to make sure gpio_get_flags() is available and that we use it:\n\ngpio_set_flags((gpio_get_flags() \u0026 ~GPIO_INPUT) | GPIO_OUT_HIGH);",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 63
      },
